  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 13pt;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Details : </strong>Jharkhand Academic Council (JAC) </span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"font-size: 13pt;\">has released the </span><span style=\"font-size: 13pt;\"><strong data-start=\"227\" data-end=\"243\">notification</strong> for the <strong data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"307\">Jharkhand Teacher Eligibility Test (JHTET) 2026</strong>. The <strong data-start=\"313\" data-end=\"339\">JHTET application form</strong> has started from <strong data-start=\"356\" data-end=\"373\">21 April 2026</strong>, and the last date to apply for the <strong data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"436\">JHTET Online Form 2026</strong> is <strong data-start=\"440\" data-end=\"457\">20 June 2026</strong>.&nbsp;Candidates who are preparing for the <strong data-start=\"630\" data-end=\"656\">JHTET 2026 examination</strong> can check all the important information related to the <strong data-start=\"712\" data-end=\"738\">JHTET Jharkhand Online Form 2026</strong> given below.</span></span></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-2\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Jharkhand Academic Council, Ranchi (JAC) </span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">JHTET Jharkhand Online Form 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Application Start Date : <strong>21 April 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date : <span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>20 June 2026</strong></span></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Fee Payment Last Date : <strong>20 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Exam Date :&nbsp;<strong>Notify Later</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Admit Card : <b>Before Exam</b></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"background-color: #ffcc00; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Fees For Paper I or Paper II Only</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">General, EWS, BC : <strong>Rs.&nbsp;</strong><strong>1300/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">SC, ST : <strong>Rs.&nbsp;</strong><strong>700/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"background-color: #ffcc00; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Fees For Both Paper</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">General, BC, EWS :<strong> <span style=\"color: #000000;\">Rs.&nbsp;1500/-</span></strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">SC, ST :<strong> <span style=\"color: #000000;\">Rs. 800/-</span></strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Candidates have to pay their Examination Fee Through Debit Card / Credit Card / Net Banking / UPI and Other Fee Payment Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>JHTET Notification 2026 : Age Limit</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">As per rules JHTET</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Use <span style=\"color: #000000; background-color: #ffff00;\"> </span>Tool – </span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>JHTET Online Form 2026 : Educational Qualification&nbsp;</b></span></h3>\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 30.4911%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Class&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 69.5089%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Eligibility&nbsp;</strong></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 30.4911%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Primary Level Teachers (Class 1 to 5)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 69.5089%; text-align: left;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"121\" data-end=\"215\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates must have passed 10+2 (Intermediate) with at least 50% marks (or 45% as per NCTE rules) along with or appearing in a 2-year Diploma in Elementary Education (BTC/D.El.Ed), or a 4-year B.El.Ed, or a 2-year Diploma in Special Education. Alternatively, candidates with a Bachelor’s degree and pursuing or completed a 2-year Diploma in Elementary Education are also eligible.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"width: 30.4911%; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Upper Primary Teacher (Class 6 to 8)</span></td>\n<td style=\"width: 69.5089%;\">\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"121\" data-end=\"276\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates must meet any one of the following qualifications: a Bachelor’s degree along with or appearing in a 2-year Diploma in Elementary Education (BTC/D.El.Ed); or a Bachelor’s degree with at least 50% (or 45% as per NCTE rules) and B.Ed/L.T./Shiksha Shastri; or 10+2 with at least 50% and a 4-year B.El.Ed or B.A/B.Sc.Ed; or a Bachelor’s degree with at least 50% and B.Ed in Special Education; or a Master’s degree with 55% marks and a 3-year integrated B.Ed-M.Ed course.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>JHTET Online Form 2026 : How To Apply</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Candidates can apply through link https://jacexamportal.in/ or provided below in link section or they can also apply through official site of the JHTET Online Form before Last Date.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">You Can Check other&nbsp;&nbsp;Notification Here –&nbsp;</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">For all the interested and eligible candidates who want to apply for JTET Online Form can read all the information related to the form is given below and the link to apply is given in the Important Link section below.</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Note – छात्रो से ये अनुरोध किया जाता है की वो अपना फॉर्म भरने से पहले Official Notification (Last Date, Age Limit, Qualification) को ध्यान से जरूर पढे उसके बाद ही अपना फॉर्म भरे।</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 100%;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"has-text-align-center\" style=\"text-align: center; padding: 10px 0px;\" colspan=\"4\" data-align=\"ce